-- Purpose: Handles all DataStore operations, Security Validation, Session Management, and prevents item duplication.
-- Production gifting hardening: final TransferTool validates Receive Gifts and rapid setting toggles are persisted reliably.
-- Runs on: Server
-- Location: ServerScriptService > TycoonDataHandler
-- Dependencies: Players, ServerStorage, DataStoreService, Workspace, ReplicatedStorage, HttpService, CarStats, BaseSkinStats
-- Public API: TycoonAdminAPI (BindableFunction), LegendaryCraftingInventoryFunction (BindableFunction)
-- Public API: TycoonAdminAPI (BindableFunction), LegendaryCraftingInventoryFunction (BindableFunction), MythicalCraftingInventoryFunction (BindableFunction)
-- Networking: TycoonAdminLog (RemoteEvent), ShopRemotes (via Bindable)
-- Security: Server-authoritative tool validation, anti-wipe protection, fixed StarterGear duplication exploit.
-- Performance: Batched saving, lock-based pad restoration to prevent race conditions.
-- Notes: Updated to support UNCOMMON, RARE, EPIC, LEGENDARY, and MYTHICAL SHOP Persistence.
--       Starter Pack ownership now lives in this main player data record.
--
-- FIX (Legendary Sacrifice Dupe):
--   Added session.SacrificeOccurred flag. Set to true whenever
--   LegendaryCraftingInventoryAPI:RemoveTool succeeds. The anti-wipe inventory
--   check is gated behind this flag so a legitimate sacrifice-to-empty-inventory
--   is never mistakenly restored. Without this fix a player could sacrifice all
--   ingredient cars, disconnect, and rejoin with both the sacrifice progress AND
--   the cars restored in their inventory (free duplication).
--
-- FIX (Cash resets to 0 on rejoin):
--   MoneyManager.GetBalance now reads Cash from HiddenStats instead of leaderstats.
--   Previously every save wrote 0 for Bank because Cash was no longer in leaderstats,
--   causing the balance to be wiped on every rejoin.
--
-- FIX (Inventory Doubles on Every Rejoin — CRITICAL):
--   The save() function previously scanned both Backpack AND StarterGear.
--   Because giveTool() places a clone in both containers, each tool was recorded
--   twice per unique type. Over successive rejoin cycles the inventory would
--   grow exponentially (3 cars → 4 → 5 → ...). StarterGear is now excluded
--   from the inventory scan; it is a within-session respawn mirror only and
--   must never contribute to the persisted inventory count.
--
-- FIX (Failed Saves Silently Drop Data — HIGH):
--   session.IsDirty and session.LastSave were reset unconditionally after the
--   pcall around executeSave, even when every retry failed. Data written since
--   the last successful save was permanently lost with no retry possible. Both
--   fields are now only updated when the save actually succeeded.
--
-- FIX (AdminAPI RemoveTool Bypasses SacrificeOccurred — MEDIUM):
--   AdminAPI's RemoveTool action did not set session.SacrificeOccurred = true.
--   Any tool removed via the admin API could be incorrectly restored by the
--   inventory anti-wipe guard on the next save. The flag is now set in all
--   three removal paths (AdminAPI, LegendaryCraftingAPI, MythicalCraftingAPI).
--
-- FIX (Shop Cleanup Not pcall-Protected → IsSaving Deadlock — LOW):
--   If any shopBindable:Invoke("Close", player) threw an error, execution
--   never reached session.IsSaving = false. The player's session would be
--   permanently locked and no future autosave would ever run. All shop cleanup
--   calls are now wrapped in individual pcalls.
--
-- FIX (Ambiguous loop variable `_` used as modulus counter — LOW):
--   RestoreLayout used `_` (the conventional discard variable) as both the
--   loop index discard AND a modulo throttle. A dedicated `padIndex` counter
--   now drives the task.wait() throttle.
--
-- FIX (Held Tool Lost on Disconnect — CRITICAL):
--   When a player equips a tool it moves from Backpack into Character.
--   player.Character is not guaranteed to exist when PlayerRemoving fires,
--   so the equipped tool could be silently dropped from the saved inventory.
--   Two-layer defence:
--     1. save() snapshots player.Character into a local reference before any
--        yielding so the scan runs on a still-valid instance when possible.
--     2. CharacterRemoving caches the held ToolId into session.HeldToolId.
--        If player.Character is already nil when save() runs, this cache is
--        used as a fallback. CharacterAdded clears the cache so a stale value
--        from a previous death never contaminates the next snapshot.
--
-- PRODUCTION SETUP NOTE:
--   This version does not dynamically create required remotes, bindables, or
--   required hierarchy setup objects. Missing required setup logs a clear error.
--   Runtime player-owned stats such as leaderstats/HiddenStats are still created
--   because this data handler owns those values during player initialization.

